  "blocks": {
    "claim-text-1": {
      "id": "claim-text-1",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Aoyang Fang",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Songhan Zhang, Yifan Yang, Haotong Wu, Junjielong Xu, Xuyang Wang, Rui Wang, Manyi Wang, Qisheng Lu, Pinjia He. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Proc. ACM Softw. Eng.",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " 3(FSE), 1605–1627, 2026. Direct accept, 87 of 920."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3797100",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PDF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://doi.org/10.1145/3797100",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "ACM DL"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04711",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "arXiv"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://operationspai.github.io/revisiting-rca-evaluation/",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Project"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://profile.aoyangfang.top/fse26-rca/",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Talk slides"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Public RCA benchmarks overstate how well root cause analysis works. On 1,430 failures that propagate like real incidents, 11 state-of-the-art models rank the true root cause first "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "21%",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " of the time; the best, MicroRCA, 37%."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "shortcut-text-5": {
      "id": "shortcut-text-5",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "SimpleRCA, a naive rule that ranks services by their number of alerts, matches or beats state-of-the-art models on four widely used public benchmarks: Top@1 0.93 against Nezha's 0.87 on Nezha-TT."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "shortcut-column-8": {
      "id": "shortcut-column-8",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "h-9",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Public benchmarks"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-10",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-11",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-12",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Fewer than 200 cases in all but one"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-13",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-14",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Faults reach 2–3 hops at most"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-15",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-16",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "99% of cases miss some fault-relevant signal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "shortcut-column-17": {
      "id": "shortcut-column-17",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "h-18",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This benchmark"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-19",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-20",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-21",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "1,430 validated failure cases"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-22",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-23",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Call depth up to 7, 84% of services reached"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-24",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-25",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "16.47 requests per second, against 0.14–4.35"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "shortcut-columns-7": {
      "id": "shortcut-columns-7",
      "type": "container",
      "layout": "columns",
      "children": [
        "shortcut-column-8",
        "shortcut-column-17"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "columnWidths": [
          1,
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "shortcut-image-27": {
      "id": "shortcut-image-27",
      "type": "image",
      "assetId": "shortcut-asset-26",
      "alt": "CPU of five TrainTicket services during CPU faults in a public dataset: only the injected services spike",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In most benchmark cases the root cause is the loudest symptom. Across 737 cases in 11 public datasets, 86% show pronounced symptoms only at the injected service, or none at all."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center"
    },
    "travel-text-28": {
      "id": "travel-text-28",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-29",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A closed-loop generator makes faults propagate, so the cause is no longer the loudest symptom, and keeps a failure only when users would notice it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-30",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-31",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-32",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Load.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " TrainTicket, 50 services, driven by a state-machine workload."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-33",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-34",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Inject.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " 9,152 faults sampled from 31 types in 6 categories through ChaosMesh."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-35",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-36",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Observe.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Metrics, logs, traces and network telemetry through OpenTelemetry."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-37",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-38",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Validate.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Z-tests on user-facing SLIs; 84.4% of first injections are filtered out."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-39",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-40",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Label.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " 1,430 cases, each labelled from the service down to the function."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "travel-image-42": {
      "id": "travel-image-42",
      "type": "image",
      "assetId": "travel-asset-41",
      "alt": "The closed-loop benchmark construction pipeline",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The pipeline as drawn in the paper."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center"
    },
    "scores-text-43": {
      "id": "scores-text-43",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-44",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The rule that scored 0.93 before falls to 0.28. The 11 models average 0.21 Top@1, and running time grows from seconds to hours: CausalRCA needs 927 s for each 8-minute window."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-45",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No single model wins every fault type. In the 262 hardest cases, the misses fall into three patterns, each pointing to what the next methods need:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-46",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-47",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-48",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Modeling bottlenecks, 47.4%.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " A model's assumption breaks: Nezha expects a fault to raise event frequency, and PodKill does not."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-49",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-50",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Scalability issues, 39.8%.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Methods slow down or fail on 50 services under real load."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-51",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-52",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Observability blind spots, 12.9%.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " The cause leaves no signal the model reads."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-53",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The benchmark, its generator and the 11 re-engineered models are public, so the next RCA method can be measured on failures that travel."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
